@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# Preflight Teams Priority — experimental single-window build
+
+This small project builds a modified Slippi Dolphin 3.6.4 on GitHub's Windows
+runner. It contains source changes and a checksum-bound patch recipe. It does
+not contain a Melee ISO, Preflight DAT/DOL files, or Slippi account credentials.
+
+The game adapter adds **Play singles → Unranked / Direct** to Preflight's pause
+menu. Teams must be queued first. When every Teams peer connects, the modified
+emulator ends singles and the game adapter attempts to enter Teams in the same
+window. This is an experimental first implementation; successful compilation
+and simulated tests do not establish live matchmaking compatibility.
+
+## Build
+
+1. Create a free GitHub account, verify its email, and create a new **public**
+   repository named `preflight-teams-priority`.
+2. On the empty repository page, click **uploading an existing file**. Open the
+   extracted kit folder, select ALL its contents, and drag those items into the
+   upload page. Keep the folder structure. Click **Commit changes**.
+3. Open **Actions → Build Windows Teams Priority test**. The upload should
+   trigger a run; otherwise click **Run workflow**. No signing secrets are used.
+4. After a green run, open it and download **Slippi-Teams-Priority-Windows-test**
+   under **Artifacts**. Extract both the artifact wrapper and the test ZIP inside.
+5. Follow the included `TESTING.txt`. Never upload your ISO or `user.json` here.
+
+If the run fails, share the Actions run URL. A failed build does not produce a
+playable release. GitHub may require account verification before running Actions.
+For a public repository, standard hosted Windows runners are free under GitHub's
+current Actions policy; do not enable paid or larger runners for this project.
+
+## Source and reproducibility
+
+`parallel-queue/dolphin.patch` applies to project-slippi/Ishiiruka tag v3.6.4
+(commit e7711b104b339a99385f2bb12b472d46140a7bc7). It includes the native changes,
+PowerPC adapter source, module builder and isolated tests. The workflow fetches
+that upstream source and its pinned submodules, applies the patch, tests the
+small Windows components, and builds the ordinary WX frontend.
+
+The original Preflight mod is by Aitch. This project is an independent
+experimental integration, not an official Preflight or Slippi release. We have
+compiled original-module exports rather than Aitch's original source tree.
+The adapter source is GPLv2+; the Dolphin patch is subject to Dolphin's license.
diff --git a/Development/SingleInstance/BuildKit/TESTING.txt b/Development/SingleInstance/BuildKit/TESTING.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7ad4e24
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Development/SingleInstance/BuildKit/TESTING.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+FIRST LIVE TEST — experimental one-window Teams priority
+
+This is a test build. Live Teams handoff has not been verified by its author.
+Use cooperative test opponents who expect the singles disconnect.
+There is one emulated game and one native controller path. No desktop helper,
+second instance, controller pipe, DTM startup recording or custom hotkey is used.
+
+SETUP (once)
+1. Extract the whole test ZIP to a NEW folder. Do not replace Slippi Launcher's
+   Dolphin. Keep all included DLLs and the Sys folder together.
+2. Copy your existing Dolphin User folder into this test folder as "User".
+   It should contain Config and Slippi, with Slippi\user.json inside. A normal
+   Windows user folder is Documents\Dolphin Emulator. Keep that original intact.
+   Never share user.json. If the source folder is unclear, skip this copy and
+   log in once in the test build instead.
+3. Double-click Patch-Preflight.cmd. Choose your original working Preflight v1.1
+   ISO, then save a NEW ISO, e.g. Preflight-ParallelQueue-test.iso.
+   The original is preserved. The patcher rejects a different unsupported ISO.
+4. Launch the included Slippi Dolphin.exe and open the NEW patched ISO.
+   Its title includes [Teams Priority test]. Configure Port 1 to GameCube
+   Adapter for Wii U for your Phob/Lossless adapter, as in ordinary Slippi.
+   Set other ports normally for your setup. Only this one instance uses USB.
+
+TEST
+1. At Slippi's online character select, use L+R to enter Preflight as usual.
+2. Choose your character/stage and enter practice. Pause with Start.
+3. Use Preflight's existing Queue menu to search Teams with your usual code,
+   EC@918. Your teammate queues normally from their own computer.
+4. Open the new Play singles menu and select Unranked. Enter a singles game.
+   Direct is available for a separate test with a cooperative opponent.
+   For this first implementation, queue Teams BEFORE starting singles. Starting
+   a Teams search from inside an already-running singles match is not provided.
+5. When ALL Teams peers connect, singles should disconnect. Allow the ordinary
+   game-end/report/replay and character-select transitions to finish. Teams
+   should then load in that SAME Dolphin window using the saved Teams choices.
+   The singles game ends; it is not paused for later resumption.
+
+CHECK
+- Native Phob/Lossless inputs work before and after the transition.
+- Teams retains the intended code, character, color and team.
+- Cancelling singles does not cancel the waiting Teams search.
+- Cancel Teams in the new submenu cancels only the parked background search.
+- An assignment alone, or a failed Teams connection, does not interrupt singles.
+
+If no Play singles row appears, verify BOTH the new ISO and the modified test
+Dolphin are in use. Stock Dolphin deliberately does not expose the new option.
+If takeover stalls, record the visible scene/mode and relevant SLIPPI_ONLINE log
+messages (especially [Parallel queue]). Do not share credentials or an unfiltered
+log containing account data. This first build does not automatically recover a
+failed Teams handoff or automatically start the next Teams search.
+
+If Slippi says the ISO is invalid, a peer disconnects, or Teams fails to load,
+stop this test and report what happened. Return to your original Slippi/ISO by
+closing this build and opening Slippi Launcher normally.
diff --git a/Development/SingleInstance/Game/ppc_restore.S b/Development/SingleInstance/Game/ppc_restore.S
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0663a91
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Development/SingleInstance/Game/ppc_restore.S
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+/* Copyright 2026 Dolphin Emulator Project. Licensed under GPLv2+.
+ * GCC -Os leaf epilogues used by these small EABI adapters. r11 holds the
+ * caller's stack pointer; saved registers live at -8/-4 and the LR at +4.
+ */
+.text
+.balign 4
+.global _restgpr_26_x
+.global _restgpr_27_x
+.global _restgpr_28_x
+.global _restgpr_29_x
+.global _restgpr_30_x
+.global _restgpr_31_x
+_restgpr_26_x:
+    lwz 26,-24(11)
+_restgpr_27_x:
+    lwz 27,-20(11)
+_restgpr_28_x:
+    lwz 28,-16(11)
+_restgpr_29_x:
+    lwz 29,-12(11)
+_restgpr_30_x:
+    lwz 30,-8(11)
+_restgpr_31_x:
+    lwz 31,-4(11)
+    lwz 0,4(11)
+    mtlr 0
+    mr 1,11
+    blr
+
+.section .note.GNU-stack,"",@progbits
diff --git a/Development/SingleInstance/Game/preflight_hooks.c b/Development/SingleInstance/Game/preflight_hooks.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..58cb9ff
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Development/SingleInstance/Game/preflight_hooks.c
@@ -0,0 +1,130 @@
+/* Copyright 2026 Dolphin Emulator Project. Licensed under GPLv2+.
+ * Adapter for the exact supplied Preflight v1.1 modules. The patch builder
+ * resolves these imports using verified module offsets, never a runtime base.
+ * EXPERIMENTAL: static and protocol tests do not establish game compatibility.
+ */
+#include "queue_client.h"
+
+typedef struct MenuRow {
+    const char *name, *value;
+    uint32_t inline_value;
+    void (*press)(struct MenuRow *), (*adjust)(struct MenuRow *);
+    uint32_t state, argument;
+    void *context;
+    uint32_t colors[3];
+} MenuRow;
+extern void Slippi_EXI_Transfer(void *, uint32_t, uint8_t);
+extern void Scene_ExitMinor(void), Scene_SetNextMinor(int), Scene_SetNextMajor(int), Scene_CommitMajor(void);
+extern volatile uint8_t scene_info[], online_mode, chose_stage;
+static PFQ_Client client;
+static PFQ_Reply reply;
+
+static int query(void) { return PFQ_Call(&client, PFQ_STATUS, 0, &reply); }
+static int ready(void) { return (reply.flags & 7) == 3; }
+static void cleanup(void)
+{
+    uint8_t command = 0xba;
+    Slippi_EXI_Transfer(&command, 1, 1);
+}
+static void probe(void)
+{
+    PFQ_Init(&client, Slippi_EXI_Transfer);
+    PFQ_Probe(&client, &reply);
+}
+
+#ifdef PFQ_PRACTICE
+extern void Original_Entry(void), Original_Frame(void *);
+extern void Original_Unranked(MenuRow *), Original_Direct(MenuRow *);
+extern uint32_t root_row_count, queue_counter;
+extern uint8_t exit_to_slippi, singles_context[];
+extern void *menu_head;
+
+static void leave_practice(void)
+{
+    cleanup();
+    online_mode = 3;
+    queue_counter = 0;
+    exit_to_slippi = 1;
+    Scene_ExitMinor();
+}
+void PFQ_Entry(void)
+{
+    Original_Entry();
+    if (scene_info[0] != 0x1c || scene_info[3] != 2) return;
+    *(void **)singles_context = menu_head;
+    menu_head = singles_context;
+    probe();
+    root_row_count = client.available ? 6 : 5;
+}
+void PFQ_PlaySingles(MenuRow *row)
+{
+    if (query() != PFQ_OK) return;
+    if (ready()) { leave_practice(); return; }
+    if (!(reply.flags & 1) && PFQ_Call(&client, PFQ_PARK_TEAMS, 0, &reply) != PFQ_OK) {
+        row->value = "Queue Teams first";
+        return;
+    }
+    if (reply.flags & 4) { row->value = "Teams failed"; return; }
+    row->value = 0;
+    /* Reuse the existing Unranked callback or Direct code-entry UI. Their
+       cleanup now operates on the new foreground, leaving Teams untouched. */
+    if (row->argument == 1) Original_Unranked(row);
+    else Original_Direct(row);
+}
+void PFQ_CancelTeams(MenuRow *row)
+{
+    if (query() != PFQ_OK) return;
+    if (!(reply.flags & 1)) { row->value = "No queue"; return; }
+    if (PFQ_Call(&client, PFQ_CANCEL_TEAMS, reply.generation, &reply) == PFQ_OK)
+        row->value = "Cancelled";
+}
+void PFQ_Frame(void *object)
+{
+    if (query() == PFQ_OK && ready()) { leave_practice(); return; }
+    Original_Frame(object);
+}
+#else
+extern void Original_Entry(void), Original_Frame(void *), Original_OnExit(void);
+extern uint8_t lr_exit;
+/* 1: restart CSS in Teams mode before activating; 2: wait for the previous
+   report/replay to drain; 3: handoff completed. Reset on each scene entry. */
+static uint8_t phase;
+void PFQ_Entry(void)
+{
+    phase = 0;
+    lr_exit = 0;
+    Original_Entry();
+    probe();
+}
+void PFQ_OnExit(void)
+{
+    Original_OnExit();
+    if (phase != 1) return;
+    /* Original_OnExit first restores Preflight's original scene callback and
+       runs ordinary Slippi cleanup. Re-enter a fresh Teams CSS afterwards. */
+    Scene_SetNextMinor(0);
+    Scene_SetNextMajor(8);
+    Scene_CommitMajor();
+}
+void PFQ_Frame(void *object)
+{
+    if (scene_info[0] == 8 && scene_info[3] == 0 && query() == PFQ_OK && ready()) {
+        if (online_mode != 3) {
+            if (phase != 1) {
+                cleanup();
+                online_mode = 3;
+                phase = 1;
+                Scene_ExitMinor();
+            }
+            return;
+        }
+        if (phase != 2) { cleanup(); phase = 2; }
+        if (PFQ_Call(&client, PFQ_ACTIVATE_TEAMS, reply.generation, &reply) == PFQ_OK) {
+            chose_stage = 1;
+            phase = 3;
+        }
+        return;
+    }
+    Original_Frame(object);
+}
+#endif
diff --git a/Development/SingleInstance/Game/queue_client.c b/Development/SingleInstance/Game/queue_client.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c7025a5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Development/SingleInstance/Game/queue_client.c
@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+/* Copyright 2026 Dolphin Emulator Project. Licensed under GPLv2+. */
+#include "queue_client.h"
+
+static uint32_t read32(const uint8_t *p)
+{
+    return ((uint32_t)p[0] << 24) | ((uint32_t)p[1] << 16) | ((uint32_t)p[2] << 8) | p[3];
+}
+static void clear_reply(PFQ_Reply *reply)
+{
+    if (reply) {
+        reply->result = 255; reply->flags = 0; reply->foreground_mode = 255;
+        reply->generation = 0; reply->capabilities = 0;
+    }
+}
+static int request(PFQ_Client *client, uint8_t operation, uint32_t generation, PFQ_Reply *reply)
+{
+    uint8_t tx[13] = {0xe6, 'P', 'F', 'D', 'Q', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0};
+    uint8_t rx[16] = {0};
+    clear_reply(reply);
+    if (!client || !client->transfer || !reply) return PFQ_UNAVAILABLE;
+    tx[6] = operation;
+    tx[9] = (uint8_t)(generation >> 24);
+    tx[10] = (uint8_t)(generation >> 16);
+    tx[11] = (uint8_t)(generation >> 8);
+    tx[12] = (uint8_t)generation;
+    client->transfer(tx, sizeof(tx), 1);
+    client->transfer(rx, sizeof(rx), 0);
+    if (rx[0] != 'P' || rx[1] != 'F' || rx[2] != 'D' || rx[3] != 'Q' || rx[4] != 1 ||
+        (read32(rx + 12) & 15) != 15 || rx[5] > 10 || (rx[6] & 248) != 0 ||
+        ((rx[6] & 6) != 0 && (rx[6] & 1) == 0) || (rx[6] & 6) == 6 ||
+        (rx[7] > 4 && rx[7] != 255))
+    {
+        client->available = 0;
+        return PFQ_UNAVAILABLE;
+    }
+    reply->result = rx[5];
+    reply->flags = rx[6];
+    reply->foreground_mode = rx[7];
+    reply->generation = read32(rx + 8);
+    reply->capabilities = read32(rx + 12);
+    return reply->result;
+}
+void PFQ_Init(PFQ_Client *client, PFQ_Transfer transfer)
+{
+    if (client) { client->transfer = transfer; client->available = 0; }
+}
+int PFQ_Probe(PFQ_Client *client, PFQ_Reply *reply)
+{
+    int result;
+    if (!client) return PFQ_UNAVAILABLE;
+    client->available = 0;
+    result = request(client, PFQ_CAPABILITIES, 0, reply);
+    if (result == PFQ_OK) client->available = 1;
+    return result;
+}
+int PFQ_Call(PFQ_Client *client, uint8_t operation, uint32_t generation, PFQ_Reply *reply)
+{
+    if (!client || !client->available) { clear_reply(reply); return PFQ_UNAVAILABLE; }
+    return request(client, operation, generation, reply);
+}
