@@ -0,0 +1,97 @@
+# Singles while Teams searches — one Dolphin instance
+
+Experimental first implementation, 2026-11-16. Target: Windows 11, Slippi 3.6.4,
+Preflight v1.1, one render window and the original GameCube adapter input path.
+There is no desktop switching helper in this implementation.
+
+## Implemented source and compiled game adapter
+
+- EXI owns a parked Teams matchmaking context and a separate foreground context.
+  Character/color/team/code/stages remain attached to the parked Teams search.
+- A private versioned EXI command (E6, PFDQ version 1) discovers capabilities,
+  parks, queries, activates and cancels Teams. Generation tokens reject stale
+  events. Stock Slippi does not expose the new menu.
+- The active netplay marker uses atomic identity ownership. A standby client's
+  construction/destruction cannot take over or clear another client's marker.
+- Successful Teams peer connections make an active Direct/Unranked game follow
+  the normal disconnect path. Ranked and Teams never yield through this policy.
+- Activation waits for ordinary foreground cleanup, online game end, report
+  submission and asynchronous replay writes. Local practice replay writes do
+  not prevent parking. Replay metadata is snapshotted before queue changes.
+- Rust opaque-device calls share a per-device gate; cleanup workers are joined
+  before the Rust device/user or ENet are destroyed. Concurrent contexts do not
+  bind the same configured netplay port.
+- Compiled PowerPC adapters add Play singles → Unranked / Direct / Cancel Teams
+  to the existing pause menu. They retain the original L+R, direct-code entry,
+  menu rendering and scene callbacks. The new submenu joins the existing menu
+  update/draw chain. The five original root rows remain, including CPU Actions.
+- A ready Teams session leaves practice or restarts the singles CSS in Teams
+  mode, performs normal cleanup, then requests activation. Busy report/replay
+  state is retried without repeatedly cancelling foreground state. Parked Teams
+  selections remain protected through its first game setup.
+
+The first test queues Teams BEFORE entering Unranked. Starting a Teams search
+from inside an already-running singles game is not implemented. The singles
+match ends; it cannot be resumed later. There is no automatic requeue or failed
+handoff recovery yet. Native Phob/Lossless access is retained by using one
+Dolphin; actual hardware timing and live matchmaking remain unverified.
+
+## Validation performed here
+
+- 114 standalone C/C++ checks: active ownership, versioned protocol/generations,
+  priority modes, gameplay/report/replay barriers, serialized Rust access, and
+  the C game client communicating with the real C++ protocol parser.
+- 129 checks executing the compiled big-endian PowerPC adapters under Unicorn
+  with mocked game/EXI services. These check relocated menu registration,
+  stock-host refusal, parking, Unranked/Direct dispatch, cancellation, readiness,
+  CSS restart, busy retries, Teams activation and preserved EABI stack/GPRs.
+- Five changed native translation units compiled against actual Slippi headers
+  to Linux objects. This is not a linked Dolphin application or a Windows build.
+- The PowerShell ISO patcher passed exact synthetic-disc byte comparison,
+  preservation of the original, existing-output refusal, altered-module
+  rejection and insufficient-padding rejection. Its successful output differs
+  only in the two patched modules and their FST size fields.
+
+No live online match, full Dolphin game transition, Windows executable or Phob
+hardware test has run here. The PowerPC tests mock imported game routines; they
+cannot establish the real game's scene ordering. The Windows build workflow is
+prepared but has not run. Treat its first successful output as a test build.
+
+## Supported input and reconstruction
+
+Base emulator: project-slippi/Ishiiruka tag v3.6.4,
+commit e7711b104b339a99385f2bb12b472d46140a7bc7.
+The original Preflight is by Aitch. Its supplied patch and compiled modules are
+not an editable source release. No upstream fork/PR has been published here.
+
+Exact input hashes and structural findings are in PreflightFindings-2026-11-16.md.
+Tools/build_preflight_modules.py rebuilds the HSD function archives from exact
+originals and our relocatable ELF32 PowerPC adapters. It keeps original code and
+global offsets, clones the root rows and a menu context, appends our code, and
+updates relevant relocations and export 0. It refuses unknown originals.
+Analysis base 0x81000000 is arbitrary, never a runtime patch address.
+
+The patched tm.dat is 98,296 bytes (+2,576); its supplied ISO has 2,584 bytes of
+padding before other.dat. The patcher checks actual layout before writing.
+Other.dat becomes 2,796 bytes. main.dol and codes.gct remain unchanged.
+Tools/make_module_delta.py packages COPY/DATA recipes with SHA-256 checks;
+Tools/Patch-Preflight.ps1 uses those recipes to create a NEW ISO, never overwriting
+an existing output or the original. No original DOL/DAT or ISO is distributed.
+
+## Build and first live test
+
+BuildKit contains the GitHub Windows build template and first-test instructions.
+The generated upload kit holds a source patch against the pinned upstream and
+our ISO patch recipe, without user credentials or game exports. The workflow
+checks isolated components on Windows, builds the ordinary WX executable and
+packages its dependencies with the ISO patcher. Original settings are copied by
+the user locally into the test build's portable User folder once.
+
+Live acceptance criteria are still open:
+
+1. Both real matchmaking contexts remain alive with the same account.
+2. Singles selection/disconnection preserves the correct Teams session/ticket.
+3. Fully connected Teams peers trigger one takeover; failed assignments do not.
+4. A real game ends, reports and closes its replay before the correct Teams lobby.
+5. Saved Teams character/color/team and native Phob inputs survive that transition.
+6. Stopping/cancelling/relaunching cleans up the right resources without stalls.
diff --git a/Development/SingleInstance/RustAccessTest.cpp b/Development/SingleInstance/RustAccessTest.cpp
